Chapter: VaultCryptoTest
  cites Secrets chapter VaultCrypto
  cites Secrets chapter SecretEntry
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Hkdf
  cites Foreword chapter Sha256
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils

 The secrets vault crypto, exercised end to end.

 This chapter never compiled until 2026-07-20, so none of it had ever
 run: encrypt-payload called aesgcm-encrypt with three arguments where
 it takes four, decrypt-payload passed the tag where the AAD goes, and
 create-team-share threw the authentication tag away because
 TeamKeyShare had no field to hold one.

 A round-trip alone cannot see any of that -- two halves that share a
 mistake agree with each other perfectly. So the assertions that carry
 weight here are the ones that must FAIL to pass: a tampered
 ciphertext, a tampered tag, and a wrong derivation must each come back
 None. Before the tag field existed, the tampered-tag case could not
 even be written down.

 The key derivation is checked against hkdf called directly, which is
 the same primitive by a different route: it pins that derive-vault-key
 passes the salt and the info string it claims to, which is exactly
 what was wrong.

Section: Fixtures

 A master key built by hand rather than through derive-master-key,
 which runs 100000 PBKDF iterations and would dominate the test.

  test-key-bytes : List Integer
  test-key-bytes = hkdf-words-to-bytes (sha256 (text-to-bytes "vault-crypto-test-key"))

  test-salt-bytes : List Integer
  test-salt-bytes = hkdf-words-to-bytes (sha256 (text-to-bytes "vault-crypto-test-salt"))

  test-master : MasterKey
  test-master = MasterKey {
    mk-key = test-key-bytes,
    mk-salt = test-salt-bytes,
    mk-hash = sha256 test-key-bytes
  }

  test-payload : SecretPayload
  test-payload = payload-new "correct horse battery staple"

Section: Helpers

  vct-report : Text, Boolean -> [Console] Nothing
  vct-report (name) (ok) =
    print-line-uni (name & ": " & (if ok then "ok" else "FAIL"))

  vct-is-none : Maybe SecretPayload -> Boolean
  vct-is-none (m) = when m
    is None -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  vct-password-of : Maybe SecretPayload -> Text
  vct-password-of (m) = when m
    is Just (p) -> p.sp-password
    is otherwise -> ""

  vct-flip-first : List Integer -> List Integer
  vct-flip-first (bs) =
    if list-length bs == 0 then bs
    else list-set-at (vct-copy bs) 0 (bit-xor (list-at bs 0) 255)

 list-set-at writes in place and hands back the same list, so a
 tampered copy has to be built first or the original is tampered too.

  vct-copy : List Integer -> List Integer
  vct-copy (bs) = vct-copy-loop bs 0 (list-length bs) []

  vct-copy-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  vct-copy-loop (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else vct-copy-loop bs (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at bs i))

Section: Derivation

 derive-vault-key must hand hkdf the master salt and the vault-scoped
 info string. Computing the same thing here through hkdf directly is
 what makes a dropped salt visible; a round-trip would not notice,
 because encrypt and decrypt would both drop it.

  vct-derivation-matches : Boolean
  vct-derivation-matches =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let expected = hkdf test-salt-bytes test-key-bytes (text-to-bytes "vault-encryption:vault-one") key-length
    in bytes-equal (vk.vk-key) expected

 Two secrets in one vault must not share a key.

  vct-secrets-are-separated : Boolean
  vct-secrets-are-separated =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let k1 = derive-secret-key vk 1
    in let k2 = derive-secret-key vk 2
    in if bytes-equal k1 k2 then False else True

 The nonce is twelve bytes, not the eight words sha256 actually
 returns. This is the assertion that catches the words-for-bytes
 confusion the DevelopersGuide warns about.

  vct-nonce-length-right : Boolean
  vct-nonce-length-right =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let r = encrypt-payload vk 1 test-payload 99
    in list-length (r.er-nonce) == nonce-length

Section: Payload Round Trip

  vct-encrypted : EncryptedSecret
  vct-encrypted =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let r = encrypt-payload vk 1 test-payload 99
    in EncryptedSecret {
      es-id = 1,
      es-metadata = secret-new 1 SecretPassword "test" "" "" 0,
      es-nonce = r.er-nonce,
      es-cipher = r.er-ciphertext,
      es-tag = r.er-tag
    }

  vct-round-trip : Boolean
  vct-round-trip =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let back = decrypt-payload vk 1 vct-encrypted
    in vct-password-of back == "correct horse battery staple"

 Negative controls. Each of these must come back None, and a
 compressor-style "agrees with itself" implementation cannot satisfy
 them.

  vct-rejects-tampered-cipher : Boolean
  vct-rejects-tampered-cipher =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let bad = __record-set (vct-encrypted-copy) "es-cipher" (vct-flip-first (vct-encrypted.es-cipher))
    in vct-is-none (decrypt-payload vk 1 bad)

  vct-rejects-tampered-tag : Boolean
  vct-rejects-tampered-tag =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in let bad = __record-set (vct-encrypted-copy) "es-tag" (vct-flip-first (vct-encrypted.es-tag))
    in vct-is-none (decrypt-payload vk 1 bad)

  vct-rejects-wrong-secret : Boolean
  vct-rejects-wrong-secret =
    let vk = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-one"
    in vct-is-none (decrypt-payload vk 2 vct-encrypted)

  vct-rejects-wrong-vault : Boolean
  vct-rejects-wrong-vault =
    let other = derive-vault-key test-master "vault-two"
    in vct-is-none (decrypt-payload other 1 vct-encrypted)

 __record-set stores into the record and returns the same one, so a
 tampered variant needs its own EncryptedSecret rather than a mutation
 of the shared fixture.

  vct-encrypted-copy : EncryptedSecret
  vct-encrypted-copy = EncryptedSecret {
    es-id = vct-encrypted.es-id,
    es-metadata = vct-encrypted.es-metadata,
    es-nonce = vct-encrypted.es-nonce,
    es-cipher = vct-encrypted.es-cipher,
    es-tag = vct-encrypted.es-tag
  }

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "vault-crypto"
    vct-report "derivation-matches-hkdf" vct-derivation-matches
    vct-report "secrets-separated" vct-secrets-are-separated
    vct-report "nonce-length" vct-nonce-length-right
    vct-report "round-trip" vct-round-trip
    vct-report "rejects-tampered-cipher" vct-rejects-tampered-cipher
    vct-report "rejects-tampered-tag" vct-rejects-tampered-tag
    vct-report "rejects-wrong-secret" vct-rejects-wrong-secret
    vct-report "rejects-wrong-vault" vct-rejects-wrong-vault
  end
